short_label: XII.18
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Spheres are to one another in triplicate ratio of their respective diameters.
----
proof:

Let the {ABC} and {DEF} be spheres, and let {BC} and {EF} be their diameters.

I say that the sphere {ABC} has to the sphere {DEF} the ratio triplicate of that which {BC} has to {EF}.

For, if the sphere {ABC} has not to the sphere {DEF} the ratio triplicate of that which {BC} has to {EF}, then the sphere {ABC} has either to some less sphere than the sphere {DEF}, or to a greater, the ratio triplicate of that which {BC} has to {EF}.

First, let it have that ratio to a less sphere {GHK}.

Let {DEF} be about the same center with {GHK}. Inscribe in the greater sphere {DEF} a polyhedral solid which does not touch the lesser sphere {GHK} at its surface. [!just XII.17]

<center>
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="540" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.18 diagram" src="propXII18.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Double reductio. Case 1: ABC has the triplicate ratio to a sphere GHK
    // less than DEF; set GHK about DEF's center, inscribe in DEF a
    // polyhedron clear of GHK (XII.17) and a similar one in ABC; by
    // XII.17.Cor and V.16 GHK would exceed the polyhedron enclosing it.
    // Case 2 (a greater sphere LMN) inverts to case 1 by XII.2's lemma.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the four spheres as circles, with the diameters
    // BC and EF; the polyhedra are not drawn. All kept. Additions are
    // transparent: faceless twins ABC, DEF, GHK, LMN of the filled circles
    // (a lit filled circle is raised over the figure, #140, and DEF's would
    // cover GHK), and octagons polyABC, polyDEF standing for the inscribed
    // polyhedral solids, lit only when the proof names them (polyDEF clears
    // GHK at rest; dragging H out toward E can make it cut GHK).
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): B, C, E, F lineSliders, the
    // givens; H (GHK) and M, N (LMN) deferred until their spheres arrive;
    // B0, B3, M0, M3 off-canvas. A, D, G, K, L are derived, listed per slide.
    var GIV  = ["ABCsphere","DEFsphere","ABC","DEF","A","B","C","D","E","F","BC","EF"];
    var LESS = GIV.concat(["GHKsphere","GHK","G","H","K"]);
    var POLY = LESS.concat(["polyDEF"]);
    var POL2 = POLY.concat(["polyABC"]);
    var MORE = GIV.concat(["LMNsphere","LMN","L","M","N"]);
    geomlib.init({
